{"name":"Light Raffia","hex":"#dacdb6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"raffia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fibrous material used for tying plants, originating from the leaves of raffia palm trees (genus Raphia)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raffia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raffia palm","blocks":[{"text":"Raffia palms are members of the genus Raphia. The Malagasy name rafia is derived from fia \"to squeeze juice\". The genus contains about twenty species of palms native to tropical regions of Africa, and especially Madagascar, with one species also occurring in Central and South America. R. taedigera is the source of raffia fibers, which are the veins of the leaves, and this species produces a fruit called \"brazilia pods\", \"uxi nuts\" or \"uxi pods\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Raphia_australis.jpg/330px-Raphia_australis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raffia_palm","wikidata":"Q133289"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://